Section 3 - Scope
(6)
This Procedure applies to:
all La Trobe research activities;
all La Trobe staff and research trainees including Higher Degree by Research (HDR) students and post-doctoral researchers involved in research;
Undergraduate and postgraduate coursework students are excluded from the scope of this Policy.

Part C - Non-Compliance with Procedure
(14)
This procedure forms part of the La Trobe
Research Integrity Policy
. The Deputy Vice-Chancellor (Research and Innovation) (DVC(R&I)) or the Pro Vice-Chancellor (Research) may determine that a breach of this procedure should be dealt with as a breach of the Research Code.
(15)
Examples of actions that can be deemed breaches include, but are not limited to:
Conducting and undertaking peer review without sufficient experience, expertise or knowledge;
Failing to declare and/or manage any conflicts of interest in line with relevant policy of the organisations you are conducting the peer review for and also of the University’s
Conflict of Interest Policy
;
Intentionally delaying the peer review process;
Using information from the peer review process without permission;
Breaching confidentiality;
Failing to separate and prevent personal prejudices, predispositions and beliefs from influencing their ability to participate in the peer review process in an impartial manner;
Being a member of the research team responsible for the research that is under review;
Not disclosing a personal or familial relationship with the relevant researcher or research team;
Having a business relationship, financial or any pecuniary interest in the research project;
Other influences which might reasonably be considered to affect their judgment of the research project.
